  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_78f96e78c54c4434a15e98e17e95bffa",
      "statement": "Each cell database lives at <watch>/<cell>/ltx/e<epoch>/db.sqlite locally and replicates to cells/<cell>/ltx/e<epoch>/ in the bucket; the epoch-in-prefix is the data-path fence, LtxRepl carries the fleet key prefix itself so two fleets sharing a bucket do not replicate over each other, and a cell is registered at activation so a fresh cell can be proven durable with no cold-start window.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/ltx_repl.rs#L1-L15",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:98cacf168cb75f1ef0cc9e82bbf59de8e8348060ec912d2460b2ab59037e6830:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/replication.rs#L1-L7",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d269f3cd6ae4a7ee21f2e2753a84262611f7a16039ef3ea9edd25d256d6a0ca6:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5549832c31374e55aa8857e49b2947ce",
      "statement": "celld_ltx::Db owns the SQLite connection: it opens in WAL mode with wal_autocheckpoint(0), holds a long-running read transaction as the checkpoint takeover, diffs the WAL against the last LTX position to write the next L0 LTX file, and runs PRAGMA wal_checkpoint modes; the capture API is synchronous because rusqlite::Connection is not Sync.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/ltx/src/db.rs#L1-L39",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:56d54461eec519a8d78a213f4fb5acfe3e1e24b70f1549f648eddec72e94b3d0:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_21ff2e9b13f84111ba5b9c85e29e602a",
      "statement": "Every LTX file starts with the LTX1 magic, format version 3, a 100-byte header, per-page LZ4-block-compressed data, and CRC64-ISO checksums; the lock page is derived from PENDING_BYTE (0x40000000) and the SQLite page size and is zero-filled on decode.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/ltx/src/ltx.rs#L16-L39",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a801e246fb9372d0280778d14e5d07fdea1bef68dbba963515c60155eedddad9:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f299f99862d84c1e96f782da2446b0e7",
      "statement": "Replica drives sync (copy each new L0 LTX file up to the replica, advancing the replicated position one TXID at a time) and restore (download the LTX files in TXID order, merge with the compactor, and reconstruct the SQLite database to a temp file that is fsync'd and atomically renamed into place); calc_restore_plan anchors on the snapshot level and walks per-level cursors.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/ltx/src/replica.rs#L1-L25",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8a9afee69b165b147173aa3fa2812165fbc1ddadb3ffc81bce2542512abff9b8:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/ltx/src/replica.rs#L57-L71",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4e17f4106fca7e77d09ab2533296b18e0439b3ed808cef5926447f093f75474b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_86ee8ec3f63746c2850f3d695b64ef1c",
      "statement": "client_for keys the replication client to the cell's epoch prefix, highest_nonempty_epoch selects the newest durable copy to restore on takeover, and epoch_replicated is the fail-closed eviction gate: never delete the last local copy of state the bucket cannot restore.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/ltx_repl.rs#L1183-L1220",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5b5076c7e014b81fa1ba6052aa0fe20c62bdf734c19c5426082d53adf647135c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_bc4bcddbdb6343ecad66213285b10970",
      "statement": "A preserved local eviction snapshot is reused only as the previous epoch's baseline (eviction removes the LTX metadata, so reopening that image would start a new writer generation at TXID 1); a clean process reload is the separate resume_local path that retains both the live database and its LTX metadata.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/ltx_repl.rs#L1261-L1279",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6acdb32b30abc578567140077b4118bde50ab36d6152bb0f11be01a2d46667e8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8cfecf7a328647bf9d4e6db7f2e9914c",
      "statement": "Compaction levels follow Litestream: snapshot level 9 for complete database snapshots and default levels L0, L1 (30 s), L2 (5 min), L3 (1 h); the Compactor merges ordered LTX inputs into one byte-compatible LTX output keeping one page per input, and ReplicaCompactor is additive — it creates a destination object and never deletes a source.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/ltx/src/compaction_level.rs#L6-L54",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:964aaf74b8172f4e50b45afb1259b815a3bf714196420cca11f80efdc68a1d81:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/ltx/src/compactor.rs#L1-L47",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:485dc2a911ab8918e1662df3bca6d23ab336c1ea358e3cb6f11d188a7f0ee42b:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/ltx/src/replica_compactor.rs#L1-L31",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f7ccfcd7aff81812e8ee9f2f8e928bee6e440da95344c7ef127f0fea259b05a7:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ba790e48fbb041e1949ec14484419739",
      "statement": "CELLD_LTX_COMPACTION is on by default: when a cell's durable TXID distance reaches CELLD_LTX_COMPACTION_MIN_TXIDS (default 256) a background attempt folds the L0 chain into an additive L1 object, and CELLD_LTX_COMPACTIONS (default 2) bounds node-wide concurrency; it must be set to 0 on every node of a mixed fleet until all nodes can read block objects.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/ltx_repl.rs#L2571-L2588",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bccdbc4d19e31276e4275c3ae91871100194a22301a0a35ef03608308c7ad80f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4d673b5d31cc47819545e529f7933d86",
      "statement": "A handoff snapshot is an L9 object so a successor does not replay the complete transaction history, and the proven additive L0 chain remains the fallback restore path after an eviction.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/replication.rs#L19-L26",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ce0caf0baa99bee9cbf7e4bc407d93b67217db2eba5c8bd5ed247eac93f2ce8b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d3365d2ad51543738a440bb1b6e2d3e1",
      "statement": "A bundle is a celld-original envelope of verbatim L0 LTX files with a CLB1 magic and a binary row footer; at rest the bucket is pure Litestream and a drained bundle leaves no trace, and the BundleOverlayClient lets compaction read bundle-resident frames while its output stays pure per-cell L1s.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/ltx_repl.rs#L1461-L1474",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:71aa9104f0365fb27dc1a1c8bf141e692ed9c525a5aaece5278aeba0e951c8a5:"
        },
        {
